Description: Draw menu icons on partial repaints at 16-bit depth
 GraphicsBuffer::paint gives Graphics the damage rectangle size instead of the
 window dimensions. YXImage::composite drops images lying outside that extent,
 so repainting a menu row loses its icon. Depths 24 and 32 bypass this path
 because formatForDepth provides Render formats for them. Pass the window
 dimensions to Graphics so the extent covers the full backing pixmap.
Author: Logan Russell <me@lrussell.net>
--- a/src/ypaint.cc
+++ b/src/ypaint.cc
@@ -1161,7 +1161,7 @@
 
     fNesting += 1;
 
-    Graphics gfx(pixmap, w, h, depth);
+    Graphics gfx(pixmap, window()->width(), window()->height(), depth);
 
     if (fNesting == 1) {
